        <styleUrl>#cat_other</styleUrl>
        <description><![CDATA[<div style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.4;"><h3 style="margin:0 0 6px 0;color:#6D4C41;">Colt Stadium, Houston Colt .45s</h3><table style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;"><tr><td><b>Edition:</b></td><td>1963-64</td></tr><tr><td><b>Category:</b></td><td>Ballpark (Retail, Services &amp; Other)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Address:</b></td><td>Old Spanish Trail and Main Street</td></tr><tr><td><b>Location:</b></td><td>Houston, TX, United States</td></tr><tr><td><b>Entry Type:</b></td><td>Listing</td></tr><tr><td><b>Archival Notes:</b></td><td>Opened	 1962. Closed 1964. In 1971, it was sold to a Mexican League team, dismantled and shipped to Torreón, Mexico. The Houston Colt .45s played here from 1962 - 1964 before moving to the Astrodome and renaming themselves The Astros.</td></tr></table></div>]]></description>
